			"notes": "## Fabric 1.16.5 crash fix\n\nFixes a server crash caused by `/c <search>` on Minecraft 1.16.5. The compatibility layer previously called the newer `Item.getName()` mapping (`method_7848`), which does not exist in the 1.16.5 runtime.\n\n- Retrieves item display names through an `ItemStack`, compatible with both supported Minecraft versions.\n- Applies the same compatibility path to pinyin search, item search, debug output, and key binding feedback.\n- Retains the complete-NBT preservation introduced in v1.5.10.\n\nVerified on an isolated real Fabric 1.16.5 server: `/c stone` opens the backpack and the server remains running without `NoSuchMethodError`.\n\nUse `sharedbackpack-fabric-1.16.5-1.5.11.jar` for Minecraft 1.16.5. It replaces the broken v1.5.10 package."
		},
