			"notes": "## Complete NBT preservation\n\n- Stores and restores every original item NBT tag without adding, stripping, or rewriting display data.\n- Keeps CTM/custom-map items, custom names, lore, `CustomModelData`, `BlockEntityTag`, map data, and mod tags intact.\n- Item merges and sorting now require the same item ID and exactly equal full NBT.\n- Removes the old backpack metadata Lore from items so the UI no longer alters stored items.\n\nTested on an isolated Fabric 1.16.5 server: a custom item carrying `display.Name`, `display.Lore`, `CustomModelData`, and `Unbreakable` survived the SQLite store/restore round trip unchanged.\n\nThe release ships Fabric builds for Minecraft 1.16.5 and 1.20.1.\n\nNote: NBT stripped by earlier plugin versions cannot be reconstructed; this release preserves tags going forward."
		},
